                            <comment id="15383764" author="zjffdu" created="Tue, 19 Jul 2016 08:11:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I guess the behavior is changed after &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-804&quot; title=&quot;Refactoring registration mechanism on Interpreters&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-804&quot;&gt;ZEPPELIN-804&lt;/a&gt;, I notice the defaultInterpreter is defined in interpreter-setting.json. &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=jongyoul&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;jongyoul&quot;&gt;jongyoul&lt;/a&gt; Can you confirm that ? If this is the case, I think we should update the document. zeppelin.interpreters in zeppelin-site.xml will be removed in future, right ?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15384876" author="jongyoul" created="Tue, 19 Jul 2016 21:22:21 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=zjffdu&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;zjffdu&quot;&gt;zjffdu&lt;/a&gt; Sure, zeppelin.interpreters will be deprecated and we will use interpreter-setting.json instead. In case of setting default interpreter within a same group, I have a plan to enable to set it in interpreter setting tab. Do you have better idea to handle it?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15385135" author="zjffdu" created="Wed, 20 Jul 2016 00:49:43 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;That make sense to me. BTW, another question but not related to this ticket,  For now the interpreter setting is globally applied,  but I think it would make more sense to allow each user has his own interpreter setting. Do we have plan on that ? I know this would involve large change, just want to raise it here.  If it makes sense, we can put it on the roadmap. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
